\title{RieszCML: Riesz Representer Based Targeted and One-Step Estimation}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Constructs asymptotically efficient one-step estimators and targeted minimum loss-based estimators (TMLEs) for statistical parameters that are linear functionals of one or more nuisance functions, or smooth transformations of such functionals. Each functional is specified through its nuisance estimates, Riesz representer, and efficient influence function using the 'RieszCurve' class; nested functionals, such as longitudinal treatment regimes, controlled direct effects, and estimands under outcome missingness or two-phase sampling, are built by chaining stages with the 'ComposedRieszCurve' class. Nuisance estimation is left to the user, so any regression procedure, including cross-fitted super learners, may be supplied. Delta-method helpers provide inference for contrasts, ratios, and odds ratios of fitted functionals.
}
